  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Download order and payload (FR-9, FR-6)",
      "items": [
        "The subtitle pass runs first; the media pass runs whatever it answered, so a failed or rate-limited subtitle api never costs the video.",
        "A pass that writes no subtitle file probes the video language once and retries in its primary subtag; the report prints 'subtitle fallback - video language <code>'.",
        "Escape during the subtitle pass cleans fresh partials, removes the work folder and returns 130.",
        "ffmpeg ships inside every glibc bundle and the macOS pkg; the preflight only locates it in bin/, then PATH, then the single-file fallback, with no offer and no run-time download.",
        "Item 9 adds --write-description to the video pass; a zero exit renames every *.description next to the media to .txt.",
        "Default and fallback downloads land in <base>/ytdlp-cli-downloads; the base is Desktop, then Downloads, then the project root; a saved output_dir wins verbatim."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Summary key (FR-22)",
      "items": [
        "s and S on the main prompt take the clipboard link; no link prints one amber line and holds.",
        "The same one-shot language fallback runs before any sound pass, so a generated-track 429 still yields the video-language text.",
        "Fresh subtitle files go through the stripper in text mode regardless of the stored stripper settings.",
        "Only a missing text result falls back to sound: a settings copy with audio only and playlist off drives that pass, so stored settings are never rewritten.",
        "The s row paints directly above the 0 row; the hint block under the box names the resolved DL location."
      ]
    }
  ]
